# POLICE-STYLE SUMMARY — CCTV cam14_stream-14 (Unknown Location, cam14)
**Footage reviewed:** 171 minutes (minutes 0–170), nighttime, timestamped in part 4 as 22:14–22:38, Saturday 13-06-2026.

## 1. SCENE
The camera overlooks a busy, well-lit urban intersection at night, with zebra/pedestrian crossings, traffic lights (cycling normally, green at minutes 0 and 20), and a side street visible (used at minute 138). Road surface was repeatedly wet/reflective, indicating recent or ongoing rain/drizzle throughout much of the footage. A "WestBank" sign was visible at minutes 160 and 165.

## 2. TRAFFIC AND PEOPLE
Traffic flowed continuously and steadily across the whole period. Observed vehicle types and colours:
- **White cars/hatchbacks** — the dominant recurring vehicle, entering from the left and exiting right roughly every minute throughout (e.g. minutes 24, 35, 43, 51–62, 64–71, 100–124, 125–148, 150–170).
- **Black sedans/SUVs/cars** — frequent (minutes 14, 37, 38, 46, 55, 71, 75, 78, 93, 95, 96–97, 105–123, 128–148, 153–163).
- **Red cars/sedans/SUVs** (minutes 20, 26, 31–32, 63, 99, 103–121, 130–145, 154, 158–164), **silver cars/sedans/hatchbacks** (minutes 7, 35, 72, 93, 129, 169), a **blue car** (minute 147), an **orange sedan** (minute 55), a **white SUV** (minute 90).
- **Auto-rickshaws** — constant throughout: yellow (most common), white, green, yellow-green, red, blue, and black, carrying passengers at times.
- **Motorcycles/scooters** — frequent in nearly every stretch, various colours (white, red, green, yellow, dark), some stopping near pedestrian crossings.
- **Buses** — red (minutes 3–4, 23, 38, 48–49, 56, 58, 65, 70, 76–77, 91, 105, 107, 152, 161), blue (minutes 28, 32, 36, 54, 67, 111, 128, 167), a large orange bus (minute 59), and a white bus (minute 111).
- **Vans/trucks** — silver van (minutes 7, 157), blue truck with goods and a person standing beside it (minute 22), red van parked right (minute 42), white van (minutes 46, 61, 104, 126, 140, 159, 168), blue pickup truck (minute 110), red pickup truck (minute 160), blue municipal garbage truck (minute 125), large blue bus/van (minute 124).
- **Pedestrians** — sparse and occasional: crosswalk users (minutes 1, 8, 14, 60, 62, 87, 94, 98, 100, 122, 144, 149), two people exiting an auto-rickshaw (minute 119), a person standing by a yellow auto-rickshaw (minute 149), a rider in a white shirt (minutes 22, 101), a man in a white shirt with rolled sleeves, black pants and helmet (minute 144). No suspicious person-object or person-person interactions observed.

## 3. VEHICLES IDENTIFIED
None identified. (The only branding noted was "GSRTC" on a blue bus at minute 36 and "Patel" on a red bus at minute 161; no vehicle make or model — e.g. Toyota, Tata — was identified anywhere; all were "model unidentified.")

## 4. REGISTRATIONS READ
All of the following are single automatic reads, not verified against any registry:
- "123456" — white hatchback, minute 24 (also read at minutes 35, 66, 104, 117, 120, 130; likely the same recurring/partially misread plate).
