## 5. NOTABLE EVENTS
- Minute 22 — blue truck with goods and a person standing beside it.
- Minute 52 — one motorcycle stopped twice near the intersection centre.
- Minute 85 — stationary white van marked "FS COURIERS & CARGO SERVICE" near centre-right.
- Minute 104 — red car reversed back into its lane.
- Minutes 108, 112 — black sedan reversed slightly before exiting.
- Minute 119 — two people exited an auto-rickshaw on the right and walked to the crossing.
- Minute 136 — black sedan stopped near a pedestrian crossing then reversed direction.
- Minute 138 — black car with blue lights turned into a side street.
- Minute 154 — red car reversed slightly then moved forward.

## 6. CROWD AND CONGESTION
None observed. Traffic flowed continuously with no build-ups, queues or jams; vehicles at most paused briefly at crossings or stopped at lights (e.g. red bus stationary at bottom of frame, minutes 3–4; blue bus stationary bottom-left, minute 128).

## 7. TRAFFIC VIOLATIONS
None observed. No wrong-way driving, helmetless riders, red-light jumping or illegal parking was reported. (Reversing manoeuvres at minutes 104, 108, 112, 136 and 154 were noted but not flagged as violations; the black car with blue lights at minute 138 was not identified as an emergency vehicle.)

## 8. PATTERN OF ACTIVITY
The scene was remarkably uniform across all 171 minutes: a busy nighttime intersection with continuous, free-flowing traffic and no alerts. The dominant pattern was a white hatchback/car entering from the left and exiting right roughly every minute — this recurred in every part of the footage and is likely the same or a similar vehicle repeatedly captured (its plate was repeatedly auto-read as variants of "123456"/"1234"). Yellow auto-rickshaws (with green, white, red, blue and black variants) and motorcycles of assorted colours formed the constant background traffic, with black sedans/SUVs, red cars, red and blue buses, and occasional vans and trucks interspersed. Wet/reflective road conditions recurred throughout (minutes 15, 21, 23, 29–32, 50–51, 58, 67, 77, 81, 84, 92, 96, 106, 109, 112, 118, 120, 155–157, 162, 164–166, 169), suggesting intermittent rain across the period. Pedestrian activity was consistently light. The only mild deviations from routine were the reversing vehicles (minutes 104, 108, 112, 136, 154), the black car with blue lights turning into a side street (minute 138), and the parked courier van (minute 85). No period was notably busier or quieter than another; volume was steady from start to finish.

## 9. QUIET PERIODS
None observed. There were no stretches of inactivity; traffic and occasional pedestrians were present in every minute of the footage, and no alerts were raised at any point.
